Problem Statement: 
To design and implement a C++ program to insert the elements 50, 40, and 30 into an AVL tree.
After inserting these elements, the program should identify the Left-Left (LL) imbalance and perform 
the required right rotation to maintain the balance of the tree. The program 
should display the final balanced AVL tree using inorder traversal.



Changed Problem Statement:

To write a C++ program to insert the elements 50, 40, and 30 into an AVL tree 
and perform the required LL (Left-Left) rotation to maintain the balance of the tree.
The program is further modified to display the tree before and after rotation, print the 
balance factors of affected nodes, and accept user input to detect whether the given sequence causes an LL imbalance.
